  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Seeds of Service: Empowering Youth Through Ethical and Structured Volunteerism</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This initiative will be implemented in phases. The current financing will support Phase I of the proposed two -year project. During this phase, project steering committees will be established at the national and regional levels in Addis Ababa, Dire Dawa, Oromia, and Amhara. Youth recruitment campaigns will be conducted across schools, universities, Civil Society Organisations (CSOs), and local authorities, enabling 2,000 youth to register in the Authority for Civil Society Organizations Volunteer Management Information System (ACSO VMIS), and a baseline study will be conducted.  This phase will provide a clear understanding of youth needs, skills, and community gaps. Transparent and inclusive recruitment will ensure equitable participation while motivating youth and raising awareness of volunteer opportunities.</narrative>
  </description>
